.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt QR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qr
.Nd encode text as a QR code, in the terminal or as an image
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l Ar level
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Op Ar text ...
.Nm
.Fl h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
encodes text as a QR code with
.Xr qrencode 1 .
The text is the arguments, joined by spaces, or else the standard
input, its trailing newlines dropped.
.Pp
Without
.Fl o ,
the code is drawn in the terminal when the standard output is one, and
written to it as SVG otherwise, so
.Ql qr text > code.svg
works.
With
.Fl o ,
the type follows the file's extension:
.Pa .svg ,
.Pa .png ,
.Pa .eps
or
.Pa .xpm ,
in either case; any other needs
.Fl t .
SVG is written compact: one path, run-length encoded, with no XML
header.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-o file"
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl l Ar level
The error correction level:
.Ql L ,
.Ql M ,
.Ql Q
or
.Ql H ,
in either case.
The default is
.Ql Q .
.It Fl o Ar file
Write the code to
.Ar file ,
or to the standard output for
.Ql - ,
as SVG unless
.Fl t
says otherwise.
.It Fl s Ar size
The size of a module in pixels, for the image types; a positive whole
number, 5 by default.
.It Fl t Ar type
The type to write, whatever the file is called: the images
.Ql SVG ,
.Ql PNG ,
.Ql PNG32 ,
.Ql EPS
and
.Ql XPM ,
or, for a terminal,
.Ql UTF8
.Pq the default there ,
.Ql UTF8i ,
.Ql ANSIUTF8 ,
.Ql ANSIUTF8i ,
.Ql ANSI256UTF8 ,
.Ql ANSI ,
.Ql ANSI256 ,
.Ql ASCII
and
.Ql ASCIIi ,
spelt as here.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The code was written.
.It 1
There was nothing to encode,
.Xr qrencode 1
is missing, or it failed.
.It 2
A usage error: an unknown type or level, a size that is not a positive
number, or a file whose type its name does not tell.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show a URL in the terminal, to be read with a phone:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ qr https://example.org/
.Ed
.Pp
Write it as a PNG, ten pixels a module, with the highest error
correction:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ qr -o code.png -s 10 -l H https://example.org/
.Ed
.Pp
Encode a file's contents as SVG:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ qr < wifi.txt > wifi.svg
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qrencode 1
.Sh CAVEATS
The SVG options
.Nm
gives need
.Xr qrencode 1
4.1 or later.
